1
00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:03.970
In this notebook, you're going to add
tracing and observability

2
00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.973
into the agent that you previously built
in the last notebook.

3
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.310
So you'll start from the agent
that you've already built.

4
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.678
And then you're going to add a few things

5
00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:15.181
in here to allow you to trace
that agent using Arize Phoenix,

6
00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.485
and then get some better observability
into what your agent's doing.

7
00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:22.555
So as before, you're going to start out
by adding some new imports here

8
00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:25.325
that will be used for Phoenix.

9
00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.962
So importing here Phoenix
as well as some basic libraries,

10
00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:33.033
and then importing a few things
from Phoenix here to set up some of that

11
00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.136
tracing observability registering here

12
00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:39.239
as well as some libraries
from OpenTelemetry, which you just learned

13
00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:42.876
about in the previous slides,
and then a library called Open Inference.

14
00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.747
Open Inference is a library
that's used and created by the Arize team,

15
00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.751
and it helps translate some concepts
in OpenTelemetry to work better with LLMs.

16
00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.121
So those are your libraries there
that you're going to be using.

17
00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.890
Go ahead and import those.

18
00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.225
And then as before, you're going to set up
your OpenAI

